From: HaeImAlan <me@haeimalan.com>
Date: Sat, 13 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: fix buffer overreads in CSA switch count event

There is no policy entry for WMI_TAG_PDEV_CSA_SWITCH_COUNT_STATUS_EVENT, so
the TLV parse infrastructure does not enforce a minimum length for the event
struct, and ath11k_wmi_process_csa_switch_count_event() then uses the
firmware-provided num_vdevs field directly as a loop bound over the
WMI_TAG_ARRAY_UINT32 vdev_ids array without checking it fits within the TLV
payload. A malformed or truncated event overreads past the array.

Add the missing policy entry and bound num_vdevs against the actual length
of the vdev_ids TLV before iterating. This board takes real radar hits and
issues CSAs nightly, so this event path runs in normal operation.

This mirrors the upstream fix (ath-next, 2026); it is absent from the
pre-6.18.39 backports snapshot in this tree (no ath11k_wmi_tlv_data_len
helper and no bound).

Fixes: d5c65159f289 ("ath11k: driver for Qualcomm IEEE 802.11ax devices")
Signed-off-by: HaeImAlan <me@haeimalan.com>
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c
@@ -159,6 +159,8 @@
 		.min_len = sizeof(struct ath11k_wmi_p2p_noa_info) },
 	[WMI_TAG_P2P_NOA_EVENT] = {
 		.min_len = sizeof(struct wmi_p2p_noa_event) },
+	[WMI_TAG_PDEV_CSA_SWITCH_COUNT_STATUS_EVENT] = {
+		.min_len = sizeof(struct wmi_pdev_csa_switch_ev) },
 };
 
 #define PRIMAP(_hw_mode_) \
@@ -262,6 +264,13 @@
 	return tb;
 }
 
+static u32 ath11k_wmi_tlv_data_len(const void *data)
+{
+	const struct wmi_tlv *tlv = (const struct wmi_tlv *)data - 1;
+
+	return FIELD_GET(WMI_TLV_LEN, tlv->header);
+}
+
 static int ath11k_wmi_cmd_send_nowait(struct ath11k_pdev_wmi *wmi, struct sk_buff *skb,
 				      u32 cmd_id)
 {
@@ -8302,15 +8311,23 @@
 					  const struct wmi_pdev_csa_switch_ev *ev,
 					  const u32 *vdev_ids)
 {
-	int i;
+	u32 vdev_ids_len = ath11k_wmi_tlv_data_len(vdev_ids);
+	u32 num_vdevs = ev->num_vdevs;
 	struct ath11k_vif *arvif;
+	int i;
 
 	/* Finish CSA once the switch count becomes NULL */
 	if (ev->current_switch_count)
 		return;
 
+	if (num_vdevs > vdev_ids_len / sizeof(*vdev_ids)) {
+		ath11k_warn(ab, "csa switch count num_vdevs %u exceeds tlv array length %u\n",
+			    num_vdevs, vdev_ids_len);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	rcu_read_lock();
-	for (i = 0; i < ev->num_vdevs; i++) {
+	for (i = 0; i < num_vdevs; i++) {
 		arvif = ath11k_mac_get_arvif_by_vdev_id(ab, vdev_ids[i]);
 
 		if (!arvif) {
